    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d100">

                <pb facs="0190" n="92" xml:id="pg92"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/272: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland (Wilson) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-06-19T18:00:00+01:00">June 19, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 19—1:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>97. Your 86, June 18, 6 [<hi rendition="#italic">1</hi>] p.m. Substance of
                    telegram delivered to Drummond
                    under conditions you mention. Massigli informed me orally last night that in the event that
                    the great powers decided to make representations to Tokyo, the French Government
                    would be willing to cooperate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
